From c88742587c49496a2e6942eb61a889143dd16942 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:44:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 55/62] generate: opt-in reuse of an idle slot's chain
 (STRATA_SLOT_CHAIN_REUSE) and of a give-back's checkpoints
 (STRATA_GIVEBACK_CHECKS)

Two gaps made long prompts read from 0 or from an old deep checkpoint although the engine held a usable prefix:
E1 - with STRATA_SLOT_PARK the root and periodic checkpoints of the conversation an idle slot served sit only in
that slot's chain, which the admission search never looked at (they reach the cache only when the slot is
overwritten, after the new prompt was read): a 123877-token sibling read from 0 in production. With the switch the
search also takes a complete, picture-free chain checkpoint that is a prefix of the slot and of the new prompt, copied
like a hit on the slot's own checkpoints; the slot keeps its chain and its pending park.
E2 - a slot that gave back all it holds kept its turn checkpoint, so the next turn fell back to the root or a periodic
point (19104 = 9964 reused, 26309 = 9964 reused, ...). With the switch its checkpoints go to the main session (moved
when the request returns to that slot, copied otherwise; nothing while a paused read waits there).
The decisions are pure functions in strata/program/slot_chain.hpp (slot_chain_test: source order, an oracle of 4000
random cases equal to the old loop with the switch off, six mutations caught). tools/cache_reuse_check.py reproduces
both on a GPU (7 legs, references by another route to the same checkpoint length). CUDA (sm_86) built only; not yet
run on a GPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
