+#!/usr/bin/env python3
+"""STRATA_SLOT_CHAIN_REUSE (E1) and STRATA_GIVEBACK_CHECKS (E2): two gaps in where a request starts reading, on the
+production config's engine (a 4-GPU layer split, --batch 16 in 4 pipelined groups, STRATA_SLOT_PARK and
+STRATA_SLOT_CKPT_MOVE on), reproduced with the switches off and closed with them on - on the solo route (GEN) and on
+the route production takes on a busy server (BGEN, an admission into a batch slot, the source slot's own too).
+
+GPU only (the engine starts on the config's cards); --self-test runs this file against tools/vision_check_fake_engine.py
+on the CPU (CACHE_CHECK_FAKE_MODEL=1), with no model and no GPU.
+
+The model has a recurrent state (GDN): a request can only continue at an exact checkpoint length or at the full length a
+session holds.  A prompt read from token 0 takes a root checkpoint at its first turn boundary of 2048 tokens or more
+(--prompt-cache-root), one every 16384 tokens (--prompt-cache-every) and a turn checkpoint at its last <|im_start|>.
+The conversations here are text, about --total-tokens long (default 20000): a system prompt of --system-tokens (2500,
+so the root is at its end) and agenda text, so each has a root and one periodic checkpoint.  Every leg has its own
+conversations, so no leg answers another's.
+
+Slots: sx = 0 (group 0), sz = row 1 of group 1, so = row 1 of group 2, sk = row 1 of group 3 (a group's window writes
+the rows below its last active one, never another group's).
+
+E1 (an idle slot's chain).  K1 is admitted into sx (BGEN) and decodes --max-new tokens; YK, another conversation, runs
+alone (GEN): the main session's checkpoints of K1 go and nothing of K1 is parked from it (sx parks it with its reply
+when sx is overwritten).  K' is a sibling of K1 that parts --sibling-back tokens before K1's end, after the periodic
+checkpoint and before the turn checkpoint: only sx's chain still holds a checkpoint of it.
+  E1s  X' alone (GEN); then X2, X1's next turn, continues everything sx holds (the slot kept its conversation).
+  E1p  A' alone; then V, another conversation, is admitted into sx: sx's image of A1 must be parked whole
+       ('parked <n> tokens ... capture=slot sx', STRATA_SLOT_PARK_VERIFY's byte comparison first); then A2, A1's next
+       turn, is restored from it ('restored <n> tokens (live)').  The pending park survived the chain hit.
+  E1a  B' admitted into sx itself (production's 'slot 8 takes ...' case): the chain hit, then at its admission sx's
+       image of B1 parked, then the copy; B2 restored from that image.
+  E1b  C' admitted into so (another group); C2 continues everything sx holds.
+E2 (a give-back's turn checkpoint).  K1 is admitted into sz and decodes; K2 (K1, its reply as the slot fed it, a tool
+result) gives back everything sz holds; K3 renders K1's assistant turn again without its thinking (the template drops
+it once a new turn comes): it parts right after K1's turn checkpoint.
+  E2s  Z2 alone; W is admitted into sz (a busy server reuses it); Z3 alone.  Without the switch the turn checkpoint
+       stayed in sz and went with W's admission.
+  E2c  Q2 admitted into sz itself (the reference: alone); WQ admitted into sz parks Q2's image from the slot; Q3 alone
+       must find Q1's turn checkpoint in that image (it went main session -> sz's chain -> the image).
+  E2k  R2 admitted into sk (another group), U alone, sz untouched; R3 alone.  Today sz still serves R3 from its own
+       turn checkpoint; the switch must keep that (it copies, it does not move, unless the request is admitted to the
+       slot it came from).
+
+The processes (--runs), each with the same requests in the same order:
+  off     the switches unset: today's REUSED (E1: K' reads from 0; E2s/E2c: K3 resumes at the periodic checkpoint)
+  ref     the switches unset, STRATA_SLOT_PARK_TEST_RESTORE=1: every idle slot's image goes to the conversation cache at
+          the next request, so K' and K3 resume at the SAME checkpoint length by another route (the RAM cache)
+  on      STRATA_SLOT_CHAIN_REUSE=1 and STRATA_GIVEBACK_CHECKS=1
+  on-e1   STRATA_SLOT_CHAIN_REUSE=1 alone (E2 legs as off; X2 says '(all it holds)' exactly)
+  on-e2   STRATA_GIVEBACK_CHECKS=1 alone (E1 legs as off)
+  old     (--old-exe) the production binary, the switches unset: every request's REUSED and tokens == off's
+  on-nd, ref-nd   (--no-draft-pair) on and ref without the MTP drafter (--mtp dropped from the config's arguments):
+          the only drafts left come from the tokens themselves, so two routes draft alike and any token difference is
+          NO-GO, not INCONCLUSIVE
+STRATA_SLOT_PARK_VERIFY=1 is set in every run (--no-park-verify: not): a slot image that differs from a plain capture of
+the slot stops the engine.  Duration, an estimate (not measured): about 97 s per engine start plus about 90 s of
+requests at production's rates, so about 3 minutes per process: about 16 minutes for the five default runs, 19 with
+--old-exe, 25 with --no-draft-pair as well.
+
+GO / NO-GO.  Deciding, for each run with the switch: REUSED == the reference's (the chain checkpoint or Z1's turn
+checkpoint) with the log line of that route; the tokens == the reference's; the requests that take the same route with
+and without the switch (K2, the E2k leg) == off's REUSED and tokens; for each run without it, REUSED == off's; with
+--old-exe every request of off == old's.  A request is never compared with a fresh read (a resumed and a fresh read may
+differ in late tokens).  The first token follows from the prompt read alone and always decides.  A later difference is
+INCONCLUSIVE where the two runs' windows may have gone apart: on the solo path when DONE's drafts accepted / offered
+differ (the drafter's K/V below the checkpoint may differ by route: a slot's image has none), and on a batch slot
+always (BDONE carries no draft counts) - except in the --no-draft-pair runs, where it is NO-GO.  INCONCLUSIVE too: the
+gap does not show with the switches off, or the reference did not take its route.  One summary, exit 0 (GO), 2
+(NO-GO), 3 (INCONCLUSIVE), 64 (usage); --out writes the criteria, every request (RESUME, REUSED, DONE, tokens, its
+engine log lines) and the runs as JSON.
+
+Exact comparisons need deterministic decoding: by default STRATA_IQ_MT_MIN=1 and --extra "--pcie-frac 0 --adapt-every
+1000000 --no-prefill-borrow --suffix-draft 0" (as tools/vision_batch_check.py).  The engine's environment is the
+config's "env" (STRATA_SLOT_PARK, STRATA_SLOT_CKPT_MOVE, ...), CUDA_DEVICE_ORDER=PCI_BUS_ID, CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES in
+the config's order, and a fresh STRATA_CONV_TIER_DIR per run.
+
+  python3 tools/cache_reuse_check.py --exe build-vrope/strata \\
+      --config /media/raid0/StrataQ38FN/linux/configs/T16-143-prod262r-vision-cpu-v2.json \\
+      --old-exe /media/raid0/StrataQ38FN/Strata/engine/strata-g3-143v2 --out cache_reuse.json
+  python3 tools/cache_reuse_check.py --self-test        # CPU only, about a minute
